
# Data to text and back under names no other module uses (native-dom-0019). A cask's bridge carries a record as host
# data text, and its generated dispatcher also imports the `file` module, whose `read` and `write` share their names
# with this package's. An import alias is rewritten to the original name inside its own file, so a file that imports
# both under two aliases still calls `read` twice and cannot say which. These two names leave nothing to tell apart.

load ./read
  find read

load ./write
  find write

load ./base
  find data
  find data-tree

# host data text to data, anchors expanded
task data-from-text
  take input, like text
  like data
  send back
    call read
      read input

# data to its long text form. The anchors are passed, empty, rather than left to their default: with `file` in the
# program a second two-parameter `write` exists, and a typed overload chooses by the arguments written
task data-to-text
  take value, like data
  like text
  save trees
    like list
      like data-tree
    make list
  send back
    call write
      read value
      read trees
